      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion in the same loop or domain",
      "extracellular": true,
      "functional_impact_measured": "NOT MEASURED for Nrxn1\u03b2 specifically. The L4 paper (Nrxn1\u03b1) used the HA-tagged construct for co-immunoprecipitation and immunostaining but no functional assay for the \u03b2 isoform at this junction is described in the clip.",
      "gene_symbol": "NRXN1",
      "insert_after_residue": 340,
      "library": null,
      "linker": null,
      "loop_run_position": null,
      "median_conservation": null,
      "numbered_against": null,
      "plddt": null,
      "position_evidence": "inferred",
      "position_frame": null,
      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "L4 names the junction 'upstream of stalk residues QTTD' in Nrxn1\u03b1. Python finds QTTD beginning at position 341 in the Nrxn1\u03b2 canonical sequence (verified: Q=341, T=342, T=343, D=344), placing insert_after_residue at 340 (S). Residue 340 is extracellular (within span 51\u2013397) and 58 residues from the TM boundary at 398, well beyond the 3-residue minimum. The stalk sequence including QTTD is shared between \u03b1 and \u03b2 isoforms; the \u03b1-isoform precedent is therefore the closest available evidence for \u03b2, classified as inferred. C353 and C363 (potential disulfide pair) are 13 and 23 residues downstream and should be avoided in any final design. L4 (PMC8024894) reports an HA tag flanked by GGQ spacers inserted upstream of stalk residues QTTD in full-length mouse Nrxn1\u03b1. The QTTD motif is present in the shared stalk region of both \u03b1 and \u03b2 isoforms. Python locates QTTD at positions 341\u2013344 in the Nrxn1\u03b2 canonical sequence, placing the junction at residue 340 (S\u2192Q). The cited paper uses Nrxn1\u03b1, making this indirect evidence for Nrxn1\u03b2.",
      "residue_after": "Q",
      "residue_before": "S",
      "residue_label": "S340",
      "residue_range": null,
      "site_id": "NRXN1-internal-340-lit",
      "site_kind": "internal",
      "source_tier": "paper",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 33586859,
          "citation": "PMID 33586859",
          "claim": "To generate HA\u2010Nrxn1\u03b1, an HA tag flanked by GGQ spacers was inserted upstream of stalk residues QTTD (see Fig 4A for stalk sequence) into mouse Nrxn1\u03b1 (splice\u2010isoform SS1\u2212, SS2\u2212, SS3+, SS4\u2212, SS5+, SS6+).",
