      "numbered_against": null,
      "plddt": null,
      "position_evidence": "validated",
      "position_frame": "ortholog:mouse",
      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_exact: insert_after_residue NULL -> 371: the paper pins the junction on human canonical P58400 (paper numbering: ortholog:mouse, construct species: mouse). Paper (PMID 31262725): \"immediately after the first two bases of Nrxn1 exon-26, in maintaining frame order, we introduced the coding sequence of two hemagglutinin motifs (amino acid sequence: YPYDVPDYAYPYDVPDYA) as well as the 34-bp sequence of a WT loxP site complemented by two additional bases to avoid a frame shift and a SpeI restriction site for cloning purposes. The amino acid sequence of the translated loxP site including the two additional bases and the SpeI site within the mutated full exon 26 reads as follows: ITSYSIHYTKLSTS.\". Audit note: Recoverable: Fig 1B prints the mouse juxtamembrane sequence ...ECPSDDEDIDPCEPSSGGLA|NPTRVGGREPYPG... with A|YPYDVPDYAYPYDVPDYA-ITSYSIHYTKLSTS|N, i.e. the 2xHA (+14-aa loxP/SpeI linker) sits between the A ending the SS5 segment and the N of NPTR. Human P58400 (Nrxn1-beta, 472 aa) has ...IDPCEPSSGGLA371|N372PTRAGGREPYP, offset 0, so insert_after = 371 (A|N), 27 residues before the TM at 398 and C-terminal of the Cys-loop (ECPSDDEDIDPCEPSS). Mouse genomic knock-in (cKI), full-length alpha/beta/gamma all carry it. Surface: live anti-HA labeling of non-permeabilized cKI neurons (Fig 2A). Function: cKI mice without Cre are viable with normal synapse density/transmission and the authors state the tagged protein 'is functional'. The ADAM10 cleavage site lies between the tag and the TM, so part of the tagged ectodomain is shed.] L2 and L3 together establish a full-length, membrane-anchored Nrxn1 conditional knock-in in which a double HA tag was tolerated in the extracellular stalk between the Cys-loop domain and the TM helix; surface detection of the tagged protein was confirmed. No single residue is named in the clip, so the site is reported at region level. The stalk in Nrxn1\u03b2 spans approximately residues 300\u2013397 (all within the computed extracellular span 51\u2013397), well clear of the TM boundary at 398. Because no residue is specified, insert_after_residue is left null per the rules for a named-loop site. Conditional knock-in mouse (PMC6683742) with a double HA-epitope tag plus loxP sequence inserted into the extracellular stalk of Nrxn1 between the Cys-loop domain and the TM region; full-length membrane-anchored Nrxn1 proteins (\u03b1, \u03b2, \u03b3 isoforms) confirmed in the absence of Cre.",
      "residue_after": "N",
