      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "The 'HA-' prefix on a full-length type-I TM protein with a signal peptide (residues 1\u201350) unambiguously places the tag after the signal-peptide cleavage site, i.e., after residue 50 (G) and before residue 51 (A), the mature N-terminus. This is the only extracellular terminus in Nrxn1\u03b2; the C-terminus is intracellular (residues 419\u2013472). Python confirms residue 50 = G and residue 51 = A. The position is topology-derived because no residue number is stated in the clip. L9 (APEX2-NRXN1\u03b1) provides additional indirect support that an N-terminal fusion on a neurexin is tolerated. L8 (PMC11622183) references 'HA-Nrx1\u03b2 SS4\u2212' as a previously characterised full-length construct. Nrxn1\u03b2 is a type-I single-pass TM protein whose only extracellular terminus is the mature N-terminus (residue 51, after signal-peptide cleavage at residue 50). The 'HA-' prefix therefore places the tag after the signal peptide, at the unique extracellular terminus.",
